Mr share through you um the by moving flat or flat duplex from semi- detached dwelling into the accessory dwelling um the new regulatory framework would mean that the there would be no requirement to meet the lot type standards of a duplex um so the new regulatory framework for those right now for example we have this happen all the time in in our in our um in our staff if we have someone who wants to convert a single family home into two units flat over flat usually um and they come in and they say "Hey can I do this?" And we say "Well do you have 80 ft of frontage?" Because a sideby-side duplex each half of the duplex needs 40 ft of frontage and

so if a property owner has uh well I guess it's this I use SD1 there's actually smaller versions in in Barry own districts so we could do a smaller version but the point is they have to have a minimum frontage in order to make two units so right now um in the MR zone I'd have to have something like 60 ft of frontage to make the smallest level of duplex to make a flat or a flat duplex so if I have 55 ft of frontage I cannot do a duplex i can only do an ADU and then I'd have to have one of the two be owner occupied whereas if I had 63 ft of frontage I can do a flatware or flat duplex and

neither one has to be owner occupied um by moving the flat or flat duplex into the ADU category now it won't matter if I have 55 ft of frontage it is an ADU instead of a duplex and therefore I don't have to meet that frontage requirement um so this actually is it would make it easier for property owners who want to convert a single family home into a duplex into a flat or flat duplex okay that that explains how it makes it easier i'm curious what kind of the tradeoff here there's there's got to be a trade-off m Mr chair the flat the flatware flat duplex already if you're doing a duplex under building code has the same requirements as the ADUs will have so

